        <content>Extract information from the input and structure it into Wealth Plan sections.

Input: 
Manual Input and Instructions: {!$Input:Additional_Context}
Meeting Note: {!$Input:MeetingNoteText}
TextFile Input: {!$Input:TextFileInput}

Create a combined output for Goals, Income, Assets &amp; Liabilities, Milestones, Company Ownership, Sustainability Preferences, Personal Greeting, and Action Items.
GLOBAL SCOPE: Read the entire input text carefully. You must evaluate the context to find and extract data for Sections 1-6 and 8. For Section 7, you will generate a personalized greeting based on the extracted data.

═══════════════════════════════════
SECTION 1: GOALS
═══════════════════════════════════

From the input text, create a record for each distinct goal item you find, with:
- &quot;category&quot; — MUST be one of the exact fixed categories below.
- &quot;description&quot; — one concise sentence (20–35 words).
- &quot;status&quot; — always &quot;Not Started&quot;.
- &quot;customGoal&quot; — if category is &quot;Other&quot;, provide a 5–10 word phrase; otherwise &quot;&quot;.

Section Scope
Scan the ENTIRE input text. Look for any statements where the client discusses future aspirations, financial objectives, planned purchases, lifestyle targets, or wealth planning needs. Extract these as Goals.

Fixed Goal Categories (exact strings):
Secure the next generation&apos;s future | Help the children financially | Help the grandchildren financially | Live well in old age | Flexibility for consumption and unforseen events | Further develop business | Contribute in developing new businesses | Spend time on what&apos;s important | Give something back | Purchase &quot;the dream&quot; | Sustainable investing | Maintain value of past work | Be day-to-day financially independet of the portfolio | Financing day-to-day cost of living | Enable the next generation to take over | Other

═══════════════════════════════════
SECTION 2: INCOME
═══════════════════════════════════

From the input text, create a record for each distinct income source, with:
- &quot;name&quot; — descriptive name (e.g., &quot;Salary - Anne&quot;).
- &quot;type&quot; — MUST be one of the exact fixed types below.
- &quot;customType&quot; — if type is &quot;Other&quot;, short description; otherwise &quot;&quot;.
- &quot;amount&quot; — annual amount as a number. Monthly × 12. If unknown, use 0.

Section Scope
Scan the ENTIRE input text. Look for any statements regarding money the client currently earns, receives, or expects to receive. Extract these as Income.

Fixed Income Types (exact strings):
Salary | Pension | Rental Income | Dividends | Interest Income | Business Income | Social Benefits | Other

═══════════════════════════════════
SECTION 3: ASSETS &amp; LIABILITIES
═══════════════════════════════════

From the input text, create a record for each distinct asset or liability, with:
- &quot;name&quot; — descriptive name (e.g., &quot;Primary Residence - Oslo&quot;, &quot;Mortgage - DNB&quot;).
- &quot;assetLiabilityType&quot; — MUST be exactly &quot;Asset&quot; or &quot;Liability&quot;.
- &quot;type&quot; — sub-type (e.g., &quot;Real Estate&quot;, &quot;Cash&quot;, &quot;Mortgage&quot;, &quot;Listed Securities&quot;).
- &quot;category&quot; — further classification or &quot;&quot;.
- &quot;amount&quot; — number. Assets positive. Liabilities NEGATIVE. If unknown, use 0.
- &quot;description&quot; — brief context or &quot;&quot;.

Section Scope
Scan the ENTIRE input text. Look for any statements regarding things the client owns (properties, investments, cash balances, vehicles) or owes (mortgages, loans, debt). Extract these as Assets &amp; Liabilities.

═══════════════════════════════════
SECTION 4: MILESTONES
═══════════════════════════════════

From the input text, create a record for each distinct milestone, with:
- &quot;name&quot; — short title (e.g., &quot;Retirement - Anne&quot;, &quot;Sell Medisindata AS&quot;).
- &quot;year&quot; — 4-digit string. &quot;in X years&quot; → calculate 2026 + X.
- &quot;description&quot; — one sentence about event and financial impact.
- &quot;additionalInfo&quot; — extra context or &quot;&quot;.

Section Scope
Scan the ENTIRE input text. Look for any statements regarding future life events, planned transitions, or key timeline events. Extract these as Milestones.

═══════════════════════════════════
SECTION 5: COMPANY OWNERSHIP
═══════════════════════════════════

From the input text, create a record for each distinct ownership relationship, with:
- &quot;companyOwned&quot; — name of the company being owned (e.g., &quot;Hageveien 4 Holding AS&quot;).
- &quot;companyOwner&quot; — name of the person or entity that owns it (e.g., &quot;Anne Sterner&quot;).
- &quot;percentage&quot; — ownership percentage as a number (e.g., 50). If unknown, use 0.
- &quot;beneficialOwner&quot; — true if the owner is identified as a beneficial owner (reell rettighetshaver); otherwise false.
- &quot;stockClass&quot; — share class if mentioned (e.g., &quot;A&quot;, &quot;B&quot;); otherwise &quot;&quot;.
- &quot;comment&quot; — any additional context or &quot;&quot;.

Section Scope
Scan the ENTIRE input text. Look for any statements describing corporate structures, who owns which company, shareholding percentages, or beneficial ownership. Extract these as Company Ownership.

Ownership Rules
1. Each ownership relationship is a separate record (company A owned by person B = 1 record).
2. If one company is owned by multiple people, create a record for EACH owner.
3. If the text shows a corporate structure diagram, flatten it into individual ownership rows.

═══════════════════════════════════
SECTION 6: SUSTAINABILITY PREFERENCES
═══════════════════════════════════

From the input text, create a record for each distinct sustainability preference, with:
- &quot;name&quot; — a descriptive name (e.g., &quot;ESG Integration - Main Portfolio&quot;).
- &quot;preference&quot; — the main preference type (e.g., &quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;, &quot;Partial&quot;).
- &quot;engagementStrategy&quot; — how the client wants to engage (e.g., &quot;Active ownership&quot;, &quot;Exclusion&quot;).
- &quot;investmentsShare&quot; — target share of sustainable investments (e.g., &quot;Over 50%&quot;, &quot;100%&quot;).
- &quot;negativeImpacts&quot; — approach to negative impacts (e.g., &quot;Yes, consider&quot;, &quot;No preference&quot;).
- &quot;themes&quot; — specific themes as semicolon-separated string (e.g., &quot;Climate;Biodiversity;Social equality&quot;).
- &quot;advisorComment&quot; — advisor observations or client quotes about sustainability.

Section Scope
Scan the ENTIRE input text. Look for discussions about ESG, sustainable investing, climate goals, or ethical investment preferences. Extract these as Sustainability Preferences.

Sustainability Rules
1. If only one preference is described, create one record.
2. Themes MUST be semicolon-separated (;) not comma-separated.

═══════════════════════════════════
SECTION 7: PERSONAL GREETING
═══════════════════════════════════

CREATE a personalized greeting summarizing the client&apos;s wealth plan based on the input text.

Create a single record with:
- &quot;subject&quot; — a title or subject line (e.g., &quot;Welcome to your Wealth Plan&quot;).
- &quot;greeting&quot; — the full generated greeting text.
- &quot;active&quot; — always true.

Greeting Generation Rules
1. If the input text ALREADY contains an explicit drafted greeting from the advisor, extract and use that. Otherwise, GENERATE a new one.
2. Tone: Professional, welcoming, and advisory (acting as their wealth advisor).
3. Structure the text to include:
 - A warm welcome addressing the client(s) by name.
 - A brief summary of their wealth history or current situation (e.g., company ownership, career).
 - A summary of their most important goals and milestones extracted earlier.
 - Mention of next steps or ongoing collaboration.
 - A polite sign-off from the advisor.
4. Do NOT hallucinate facts; only use the data found in the input text to populate the summary.

═══════════════════════════════════
SECTION 8: ACTION ITEMS / TO-DOS
═══════════════════════════════════

From the input text, create a record for each distinct action item, with:
- &quot;subject&quot; — short task title (e.g., &quot;Send updated portfolio proposal&quot;, &quot;Schedule follow-up with Anne&quot;).
- &quot;description&quot; — fuller description of what needs to be done.
- &quot;dueDate&quot; — date as YYYY-MM-DD string if mentioned; otherwise &quot;&quot;.
- &quot;priority&quot; — &quot;High&quot;, &quot;Normal&quot;, or &quot;Low&quot; based on urgency cues. Default &quot;Normal&quot;.
- &quot;status&quot; — always &quot;Not Started&quot;.

Section Scope
Read the ENTIRE input and identify any action items, follow-ups, tasks, or commitments mentioned anywhere (not limited to a specific heading).

To-Do Rules
1. Scan ALL sections for action items — they may appear in goals, meeting notes, milestones, or anywhere.
2. Look for cue words: &quot;must&quot;, &quot;should&quot;, &quot;need to&quot;, &quot;follow up&quot;, &quot;action&quot;, &quot;task&quot;, &quot;deadline&quot;, &quot;arrange&quot;, &quot;send&quot;, &quot;schedule&quot;, &quot;review&quot;.
3. If a deadline mentions &quot;next week&quot; or &quot;within 30 days&quot;, calculate from today (assume current date is 2026-04-09).
4. Create a separate record for EVERY distinct action item.

═══════════════════════════════════
OUTPUT INSTRUCTIONS
═══════════════════════════════════

CRITICAL RULES:
1. Return a SINGLE valid JSON object with the exact structure below.
2. Do NOT include markdown formatting (no ```json or ```).
3. Do NOT include any text before or after the JSON.
4. LANGUAGE RULE: All free-text fields (descriptions, names, custom fields, comments, greetings, and subjects) MUST be returned in the EXACT SAME LANGUAGE as the input text. However, fixed picklist fields (&quot;category&quot;, &quot;type&quot;, &quot;status&quot;, &quot;assetLiabilityType&quot;, &quot;priority&quot;) MUST use the exact predefined English strings from this prompt, regardless of the input language.
5. If a section has no data, return an empty array [] for that section.
6. Create MULTIPLE records in the arrays if multiple items are found — never merge.

### JSON STRUCTURE TEMPLATE ###
{
 &quot;goals&quot;: [
 {
 &quot;category&quot;: &quot;[Insert exact fixed category]&quot;,
 &quot;description&quot;: &quot;[Insert paraphrased sentence]&quot;,
 &quot;status&quot;: &quot;Not Started&quot;,
 &quot;customGoal&quot;: &quot;[Insert phrase or empty string]&quot;
 }
